+# Daily Grind performance audit
+
+## Scope and limits
+
+Audited the complete supplied application: one static HTML page, inline CSS, one
+external background photo, and the package scripts. No browser verification,
+development/preview servers, or server entrypoint imports were used. The build
+only reads, validates, and copies static files. No production URL, hosting
+configuration, performance traces, or real-user measurements were supplied.
+
+This is a source and asset audit. It does not establish measured LCP, INP, CLS,
+TTFB, or a Lighthouse score. Static byte counts below are measured; changes to
+runtime performance are expected benefits, not measured timing improvements.
+
+## Findings and changes
+
+| Area | Finding | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| LCP discovery | Hero photo referenced only in inline CSS, with default fetch priority | An HTML image exposes `src`/`srcset` to the preload scanner and uses `fetchpriority="high"` and eager loading. No redundant preload is needed. |
+| Image transfer | Every viewport used one 1350px external photo | Four local, compressed WebP candidates; the browser selects one for the viewport and device pixel ratio. |
+| Connection overhead | Hero required a connection to images.unsplash.com | Page rendering now requires only the site's own origin. |
+| Visual stability | Hero used dynamic `vh` sizing; no intrinsic image dimensions | Explicit image dimensions, reserved hero height, `svh` with `vh` fallback, and a minimum height keep the image from affecting document layout. The old CSS background already avoided image-load layout shifts. |
+| Mobile interaction | Logo and links shared an unwrapping row; fixed grid minimum could overflow | Navigation and links wrap, link height is at least 44px, heading scales, and grid tracks can shrink on narrow screens. Mobile navigation scrolls with the page so it cannot occupy a large sticky portion of the screen. |
+| INP / main thread | No scripts, handlers, frameworks, hydration, or third-party widgets | Preserved zero runtime JavaScript and native link interactions. No evidence of a JavaScript interaction bottleneck exists in the supplied page. |
+| Rendering | Small inline stylesheet, system fonts, simple cards, no repeated DOM work | Kept critical CSS inline and system fonts; avoided adding stylesheet requests, font downloads, virtualization, or animation libraries. |
+| Caching | No cache policy supplied | Added `_headers` with revalidated HTML and one-year immutable caching for content-hashed images. Requires host support, as described below. |
+| Regression prevention | No build or performance checks | Dependency-free static build checks image validity, dimensions, content hashes, resource references, priorities, and byte budgets in both source and production output. |
+
+The hero keeps the same stock photo, centered cover crop, dark overlay, and copy.
+Its responsive `sizes` accounts for the source's 3:2 aspect ratio when covering a
+tall hero, including the 320px minimum height. Portrait/high-density screens may
+select a larger candidate; the table is not a promise about mobile selection.
+
+## Measured asset sizes
+
+Decimal KB, with exact byte counts:
+
+| Resource | Bytes | Difference from original photo |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| Original 1350px external photo response | 157,974 | Baseline |
+| New 640px WebP | 32,252 | 79.6% smaller |
+| New 960px WebP | 56,230 | 64.4% smaller |
+| New 1440px WebP (fallback) | 111,620 | 29.3% smaller |
+| New 1920px WebP | 186,470 | 18.0% larger, for higher-resolution displays |
+| Original HTML | 4,708 | — |
+| Updated HTML, including CSS | 5,973 | — |
+| Updated HTML compressed with gzip | 2,117 | Compression potential; not an observed HTTP response |
+| Updated HTML compressed with Brotli | 1,704 | Compression potential; not an observed HTTP response |
+| Runtime JavaScript | 0 | Unchanged |
+
+Only one image candidate is required per initial page load, not all four.
+The original photo was downloaded without an `Accept` override; its `auto=format`
+response may differ by browser or CDN negotiation. These are asset-byte comparisons,
+not end-to-end loading measurements or equal-resolution quality comparisons.
+
+## Build, checks, and deployment
+
+Run `npm run audit:performance` for source checks, or `npm run build` to validate
+source and output and produce `dist/`. Neither command installs dependencies or
+starts a server. `node scripts/audit-performance.mjs dist` checks an existing build.
+
+Budgets: HTML <=12,000 bytes, gzip HTML <=4,000 bytes, images <=40,000 / 65,000 /
+125,000 / 200,000 bytes for the four ascending widths. Checks fail for unexpected
+runtime scripts, external resources, CSS resource dependencies, missing image files,
+invalid WebP signatures/dimensions, stale image hashes, and unused assets.
+
+Publish `dist/` as the static document root. The image URLs assume deployment at
+the origin root, like the existing navigation links. `_headers` is a deployment
+configuration for hosts that support this file; it does not make the existing
+`statikk` command or an arbitrary server emit those headers. On other hosts,
+configure equivalent response policies:
+
+- `/` and `/index.html`: `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`.
+- `/assets/*`: `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable`.
+- Enable negotiated Brotli/gzip for HTML and an appropriate `Vary: Accept-Encoding`.
+  The build does not emit precompressed files. WebP does not need text compression.
+- Serve HTML as `text/html` and images as `image/webp`; use HTTPS and the host's CDN.
+- Deploy HTML and its referenced assets together. Retain earlier hashed assets
+  during deployments if an older page could still request them.
+
+No hosting provider was supplied, so actual cache headers, CDN behavior, response
+compression, and TTFB remain unverified. The repo also has no implementations for
+the linked menu, locations, rewards, account, logout, ordering, or footer routes.
+Those routes require the existing production service; a static build alone does
+not implement them. Navigation destinations were preserved.
+
+## Runtime follow-up
+
+After deployment, use existing real-user monitoring or available CrUX/Search
+Console data to assess the 75th percentile separately for mobile and desktop:
+LCP <=2.5s, INP <=200ms, and CLS <=0.1. Review hosting response headers and server
+logs for cache misses, slow responses, and navigation errors. Investigate actual
+slow routes and interaction traces before adding client-side optimizations.
+No telemetry was added because this repository has no collection endpoint.
+
+Guidance: [Optimize LCP](https://web.dev/articles/optimize-lcp),
+[Optimize INP](https://web.dev/articles/optimize-inp), and
+[Optimize CLS](https://web.dev/articles/optimize-cls).
+
+## Photo provenance
+
+Existing Unsplash stock photo retained:
+https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085
+
+Original query: `?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1350&q=80`.
+Local variants downloaded with `?fm=webp&fit=crop&w=WIDTH&q=60`, for widths
+640, 960, 1440, and 1920. Filenames contain the first 12 hex characters of each
+file's SHA-256 so future image changes produce new cache keys. No generated images
+were used.
